{"title":"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005/Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Compute the largest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5d23b6f717ba85ee1a4ae7a094310f9002d7c5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2004^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c47d07b2d07f9731fb8a26ed5472d07cfc1487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2004!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a real number with the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30eb72201432328ca51631b4db71a365f72f3a8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + \\frac{1}{x} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56f7cd18232c10f3224b02661b7e6c32c5190368.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_m = x^m + \\frac{1}{x^m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"118\" height=\"37\" />.  Determine the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b29699446f0faca3d3e99da1ee5cf1ec0ca70aa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a box, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> green balls, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blue balls, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red balls, a brown ball, a white ball, and a black ball.  These balls are randomly drawn out of the box one at a time (without replacement) until two of the same color have been removed.  This process requires that at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> balls be removed.  The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> balls are drawn can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/b/d7b64aa7cf5cfdc65f0188fd08298f9378b6b0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S := \\{5^k | k \\in \\mathbb{Z}, 0 \\le k \\le 2004\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"236\" height=\"20\" />.  Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f8e0836be8b74921931569b0f3ec901d4a97d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{2004}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d1f265f87c2649f0c2722efc85558c071c55fc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1401$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> digits, how many elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> begin with the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/860dc7662bfbc0a83d1e703f62610e7c2ce3390c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{n} = 0.d_1d_2d_3d_4\\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"143\" height=\"37\" />, an infinite decimal that has the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245551e06664fe19f066db1c096c6b8efbb1a5c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i = d_{i+12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />.  Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e61ce09efe3f712dc81b4013adc833fb23dbb813.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9901$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is prime, how many positive integers are in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />?  (The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1544d77330dc5a289ad6a42beeb236b8dd70a9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> are digits.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a scalene triangle.  Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are selected on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb0f1d8a43539dbc3355734bafb2bfd855b5f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CA}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.  The cevians <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc7f4fd0e5897e8ac812a9a562556b8cdd87341f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CF}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> concur at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  If the areas of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2f58fcb6a4d5c7a4e266914190e28cba4e2577f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ce7c52450ed6479da207f826be90f68de3c8075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FBP$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab244622ea70d566184e386740fbd215b9cf55f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CEP$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb4795bbf9125d08b3ddc9fbe238166da3bb450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$126$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/8/848ec5b5f695afbacb864efead154761481780c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, then determine the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Anders, Po-Ru, Reid, and Aaron are playing Bridge.  After one hand, they notice that all of the cards of two suits are split between Reid and Po-Ru's hands.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> denote the number of ways <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cards can be dealt to each player such that this is the case.  Determine the remainder obtained when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. (Bridge is a card game played with the standard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28dcb5d2f68ac3e60a870a7711efb58f2bcbfbe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52-$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />card deck.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the remainder obtained when the expression\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/2432b88bdbb249cbe5572b81ede9d2403dc9cb3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2004^{2003^{2002^{2001}}}\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"22\" />\nis divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092928297b4167c1a390bacffc6226923c6b3f15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(1 + x^3\\right)\\left(1 + 2x^{3^2}\\right)\\cdots\\left(1 + 1997x^{3^{1997}}\\right) = 1 + a_1x^{k_1} + a_2x^{k_2} + \\cdots + a_mx^{k_m}\\]\" width=\"553\" height=\"32\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1ec16d218e72282537122f7e6a2b641e94eba0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1eb239ac02729483468bf9d79708b9b1db6d21f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1 &lt; k_2 &lt; \\cdots &lt; k_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"15\" />.  Determine the remainder obtained when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01cf8f4cf8d0916ff1f466f213c12473453a36d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> is a cyclic pentagon with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7abe4deafa7d65ecd5721f7ab789b7354005acca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = CD = DE$\" width=\"137\" height=\"12\" />.  The diagonals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />.  We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e064fcde9dc4ccefa123647537b77b0e825ae87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA = 25$\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/707ee619459430f2a1abf044ef12b9acb70d98ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD = 113$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374f57f56338e0ad3212ed5a5b5fad7c97b8992b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" />.  [<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />] can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Determine the remainder obtained when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/2/75212ff6ab19289ae214e99f1f22526e34f9023f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x-200)(4x+1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />.  Let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/1/771ca53964ba6a24a9bbc5074c5fb872f50c5707.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\omega = \\tan^{-1}(\\alpha) + \\tan^{-1}(\\beta) + \\tan^{-1}(\\gamma).\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"19\" />\nThe value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fa0a0e873426976a635b5ace19eef7a3b2c5b91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\omega)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Determine the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd4babab25c9e82e2e8c30b21a070981213d4a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95c180b12878c1f359607e0af47b48fcf4950d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/81729cf4848260b6feda8ea5ae3f1d0867c890eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e43ab3616df7169cf742ede9da39ff3dc2ef38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA = 7$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> denote the circumcenter and intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> respectively.  The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f254a6e559e5211c72e633c720ad5ca6cc8c6a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP^2$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Determine the remainder obtained when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is the polynomial of minimal degree that satisfies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91062407a36a4480e60ea6cf3a9a76554e91d08.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(k) = \\frac{1}{k(k+1)}\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"41\" />\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8b751dc3c81ea71b1a0d2b8ce7ed7ac457d6373.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1, 2, 3, \\dots, 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />.  The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/9/20971d06479da16fa586686dc7a948c359d8d64c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(11)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/757abff905a31b8b5fa8de2f991e34003a3ffd08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"32\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> Elm trees, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> Dogwood trees, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> Oak trees are to be planted in a line in front of a library such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/5/ea55a26c17dd282c60977262d59cf3f961e09f6a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}  \\text{i)} &amp; \\text{No two Elm trees are next to each other.} \\hspace{6 mm} \\\\  \\text{ii)} &amp; \\text{No Dogwood tree is adjacent to an Oak tree.} \\\\  \\text{iii)} &amp; \\text{All of the trees are planted.} \\hspace{27 mm} \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"363\" height=\"67\" />\nHow many ways can the trees be situated in this manner?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In 